66,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"Oh dear, poor Minako. It is so heartbreaking to see her go. I hope we can find peace and the truth now.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Minako was too controlling of the conversation, which often signals a desire to manipulate the outcome. Her execution was a logical risk.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"A regrettable necessity if we suspect manipulation. However, we must note that no one was attacked last night. That is a curious detail.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"See! I told you she was acting weird! I'm just glad we're all still friends. But wait, why didn't the werewolf attack anyone?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,2,2,talk,Shizue,,Perhaps the werewolf felt a moment of hesitation? Or maybe they were simply too sad to attack after Minako left us.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shizue, that is an emotional interpretation, not a logical one. A werewolf who doesn't attack is either making a mistake or playing a very deep game.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,Or perhaps the werewolf is trying to appear harmless by not creating more casualties. It is a sophisticated strategy to build trust through inaction.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"That's a scary thought! @Benjamin, you're really good at this. Are you sure you're not the werewolf? You know too much about their strategies!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"Let's not start pointing fingers again, Kenji. It makes my heart ache to see you all suspecting each other so quickly.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,@Kenji's observation is a common pattern. The person who explains the enemy's logic often understands it because they are using it. Benjamin is very analytical.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"A classic paradox, Mizuki. The expert on the enemy is often mistaken for the enemy. However, my goal is the village's victory, and logic is my only tool.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"I don't know... @Mizuki, you're also really analytical. You and Benjamin are like two peas in a pod. Maybe you're working together?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I believe in the goodness of everyone here. Let us just try to be honest with one another. I'm sure we can solve this together.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, the ""Possessed"" role exists to support the werewolf. If Benjamin and I were a team, we would be coordinating our votes more effectively.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,Precisely. Our independent analyses are more indicative of Villagers than a coordinated werewolf-possessed pair. I believe the threat lies elsewhere.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I'm just trying to help! I'll trust you guys for now, but I'm keeping my eyes open. I'm not letting anyone trick me!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
